diff --git a/docs/CUSTOM_CURSORS.md b/docs/CUSTOM_CURSORS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..71c377b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CUSTOM_CURSORS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Custom cursor images
+
+`CursorImages` owns immutable, top-down, straight-alpha sRGB representations.
+Each `CursorImage` has pixel width, height, scale and `std::vector<Color> rgba`.
+The common logical size is `width / scale` by `height / scale`. A single hotspot
+uses fractions of that logical width and height, measured from the top-left.
+For example, the contact pixel `(3,3)` in a 32-pixel cursor has hotspot
+`(3.0/32, 3.0/32)`. Fractions must be finite and in `[0,1)`.
+
+```cpp
+std::vector<gui_forms::CursorImage> variants;
+// Supply owned RGBA representations in strictly increasing scale order.
+variants.push_back({32, 32, 1.0, pixels_32});
+variants.push_back({64, 64, 2.0, pixels_64});
+gui_forms::CursorImagesPtr cursor = gui_forms::CursorImages::create(
+    std::move(variants), 3.0 / 32, 3.0 / 32);
+control.set_custom_cursor(cursor, gui_forms::CursorKind::crosshair);
+// Restore a stock role, or nullopt to inherit the parent's whole cursor.
+control.set_cursor(gui_forms::CursorKind::arrow);
+```
+
+The factory rejects missing or oversized buffers, mismatched logical sizes,
+nonfinite/out-of-range scales, duplicate or unordered scales and invalid
+hotspots. It accepts at most eight representations, at most 256 pixels per
+axis and 256 logical pixels per axis. It throws `std::invalid_argument` for
+invalid input. Consumers loading optional assets should catch errors and select
+a stock role. A fully transparent image can intentionally hide a pointer within
+a control; restore it with `set_cursor`, without global hide/unhide counters.
+
+The host chooses the smallest source representation at or above the display
+scale, then performs common nearest-neighbor sampling to the requested physical
+size. Sampling is anchored at the rounded contact pixel so a narrow nib does
+not disappear under its hotspot. Dimensions remain bounded to 256 pixels. This
+is a pixel-art policy; callers can supply authored representations to control
+appearance. AppKit receives a multi-representation NSImage with the original
+logical size and hotspot in points. Win32 and X11 receive the common prepared
+raster and rounded physical-pixel hotspot.
+
+Each native service caches up to 32 cursor handles, owning image references so
+pointer identities cannot be recycled under a live cache entry. Repeated mouse
+movement reuses the prepared raster and native handle. Reaffirming an installed
+cursor does not advance the snapshot's cursor-change counter. Native failures
+are remembered for the most recently failed image/scale and fall back to the
+requested system role. Unsupported hosts use the same fallback. The returned
+success status means a usable pointer was installed; it does not prove that the
+host displayed a custom image. Thread and shutdown checks remain authoritative.
+
+An explicit stock cursor on a child overrides its parent's image. Pointer
+capture keeps the captured control's cursor while dragging outside its bounds.
+AppKit also projects the cursor through its tracking-area cursor-update callback,
+so system cursor refreshes use the retained control state.
+Returning to the stock fallback clears a custom cursor even when its enum role
+has not changed. Windows keeps its ordinary arrow in the native class-cursor
+path. Native caches release their owned resources at service shutdown; stock
+shared resources are never destroyed.
+
+## Platform coverage
+
+- AppKit: NSCursor over a multi-representation NSImage; straight RGBA data.
+- Win32: CreateDIBSection/CreateIconIndirect, with premultiplied BGRA and a
+  monochrome mask; stock LoadCursor fallback.
+- Linux: optional Xcursor ARGB support in the existing X11 host, including
+  operation under XWayland. Builds without Xcursor retain font cursors.
+  A direct Wayland host/surface implementation is not introduced here.
+- Headless: validated service request followed by stock-cursor fallback.
+
+Focused checks live in `tests/cursor_image_tests.cpp`,
+`tests/macos_host_close_tests.mm`, `tests/windows_cursor_tests.cpp` and
+`tests/x11_cursor_tests.cpp`. X11 checks require an X server, such as Xvfb.
+
+Native API references: [AppKit hotspot coordinates](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit/nscursor/hotspot),
+[Win32 cursor creation and bitmap ownership](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winuser/nf-winuser-createiconindirect),
+[nonshared cursor destruction](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winuser/nf-winuser-destroycursor),
+and [Xcursor](https://www.x.org/releases/current/doc/man/man3/Xcursor.3.xhtml).
